{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>הן אני</b> — four with juxtaposition-readings in the Masorah: here. And the others: הן אני כפיך לאל (Exodus 7:1). הן אני נשארתי לבדי (Isaiah 51:9 — \"I alone remain\"). And let not the eunuch say הן אני עץ יבש (Isaiah 56:3 — \"I am a dry tree\"). Moses said הן אני ערל שפתים (\"I am of uncircumcised lips\") and HaShem said to him הן אני כפיך לאל — i.e., do not worry about the circumcision of your lips, for I will be with your mouth and I will teach you. And similarly, let not the eunuch say הן אני עץ יבש — let him not say in his heart 'Who will give birth to me these?' — i.e., let him trust in HaShem that it is in His hand to heal him, and Zion will give birth."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The phrase הכא ('here') marks the present occurrence at Exodus 6:30; the other three references are identifiable but unaddressed in the source, so they are rendered without inline addresses per the discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:08.282168252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}